  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Samoa Chamber of Commerce and Industry (SCCI) has actively advocated for strengthening the policy frameworks, capacity and statistics and analysis. The ILO provides technical and financial support towards the review of the Samoa Chamber of Commerce and Industry Strategic Plan and Monitoring Framework. In addition, ILO is also supporting the research on the Impacts of labour migration on the private sector which will inform initiatives on skilling, re-skilling and job matching. Ongoing capacity building opportunities are provided both virtually and face to face for representatives of workers organizations and SCCI. These aim to increase capacities of employers organizations to participate effectively in the development of social and labour policies, programmes and advocate for their members.</narrative>
  </description>
